    "blocks":[
      {"id":"title","type":"markdown","layout":"full","body":"# Application-Style Broad Corpus — Iteration 023"},
      {"id":"summary","type":"markdown","layout":"full","sourceId":"application_results","body":"## Technical summary\n\n**Parley tied final correctness on richer applications but did not reach strict parity.** All three languages passed 48/48 hidden tasks. Parley passed 33/48 on the first check and used a median **13.46k reported tokens per task**, versus Python's 6.24k and Rust's 6.58k. The frozen gate finished 1/4."},
      {"id":"metrics","type":"metric-strip","layout":"full","cardIds":["sessions_card","tasks_card","hidden_card","gate_card","first_card","repair_card","file_card","multiple_card"]},
      {"id":"scope","type":"markdown","layout":"full","sourceId":"application_results","body":"## New application scope\n\nAll eight task IDs and statements are unused in iterations 001–022. The corpus covers invoice aggregation, mutable support tickets, configuration overlays, access policy, room scheduling, shipment state transitions, contact merging, and verified file-backed notes. Each language received the same statements, case order, and six fresh complete-bundle sessions under `gpt-5.6-sol`."},
      {"id":"effort","type":"markdown","layout":"full","sourceId":"application_results","body":"## Repairs keep agent effort above both baselines\n\nParley's 13.46k median tokens per task was **2.16× Python** and **2.04× Rust**. Median elapsed time was 11.43 seconds per task versus 6.66 and 9.43. Parley used nine repair turns; both baselines were first-check perfect. Every Parley replicate exceeded both baseline medians, so the gap is not one outlier."},
      {"id":"token_chart_block","type":"chart","chartId":"token_chart","layout":"full"},
      {"id":"session_chart_block","type":"chart","chartId":"session_chart","layout":"full"},
      {"id":"reliability","type":"markdown","layout":"full","sourceId":"application_results","body":"## Complete recovery, but no clean Parley session\n\nFinal hidden correctness was 144/144 across languages. First-check reliability was 68.75% for Parley and 100% for Python and Rust. No Parley session passed all eight tasks initially, so the preregistered repair-free sensitivity analysis is unavailable."},
      {"id":"reliability_chart_block","type":"chart","chartId":"reliability_chart","layout":"full"},
      {"id":"task_chart_block","type":"chart","chartId":"task_chart","layout":"full"},
      {"id":"file","type":"markdown","layout":"full","sourceId":"application_results","body":"## Real file behavior passed every hidden case\n\nThe harness deleted `file_backed_notes.txt` before each run and compared exact UTF-8 contents afterward. Python and Rust passed the file task on the first check in all six sessions. Parley repaired it in all six, then passed 6/6 hidden task judgments and all 24 exact hidden file cases. Across languages, all 72 exact file cases passed."},
      {"id":"file_table_block","type":"table","tableId":"file_table","layout":"full"},
      {"id":"failure","type":"markdown","layout":"full","sourceId":"application_results","body":"## No failure signature clears both independence gates\n\nFive ticket failures in five sessions assumed that `for each priority from 5 to 1` iterates downward, but this is one task family. Four join-precedence failures crossed four tasks but all came from one session. File failures split into three indexed-repeat drafts, two nonexistent `newline` identifiers, and one unwrapped file-read maybe—all one task family. Event count alone is not a language-design mandate."},
      {"id":"signature_chart_block","type":"chart","chartId":"signature_chart","layout":"full"},
      {"id":"boundary","type":"markdown","layout":"full","sourceId":"application_results","body":"## No compiler or skill change follows\n\nDescending ranges could be useful in isolation, but one ordering task does not establish a language-wide need or settle semantics such as inclusivity and zero-step behavior. Indexed repeat duplicates range loops; `newline` is not a declared value; file reads deliberately return maybes; and the join failures are one session's missing parentheses. Under the frozen stop rule, none advances to implementation."},
      {"id":"source","type":"markdown","layout":"full","sourceId":"application_results","body":"## Parley source is close to Python-sized and far shorter than Rust\n\nMedian generated source was about 206 rough tokens per task for Parley, 200 for Python, and 366 for Rust. Parley was only 3.09% larger than Python and **43.58% shorter than Rust**, yet used more than twice the agent tokens of either. The bottleneck is language recall and first-check repair, not emitted program length."},
      {"id":"source_chart_block","type":"chart","chartId":"source_chart","layout":"full"},
      {"id":"language_table_block","type":"table","tableId":"language_table","layout":"full"},
      {"id":"task_table_block","type":"table","tableId":"task_table","layout":"full"},
      {"id":"signature_table_block","type":"table","tableId":"signature_table","layout":"full"},
      {"id":"audit_table_block","type":"table","tableId":"audit_table","layout":"full"},
      {"id":"session_table_block","type":"table","tableId":"session_table","layout":"full"},
      {"id":"methodology","type":"markdown","layout":"full","sourceId":"application_results","body":"## Frozen methodology\n\n- **Matrix:** 18 fresh sessions, eight tasks, three languages, six complete-bundle replicates, seed `20260809`.\n- **Toolchain:** Parley 0.3.155 at frozen harness commit `8f4a668`, `gpt-5.6-sol` medium, Codex CLI 0.146.0.\n- **Instruction:** unchanged 1,519-character skill, SHA `6ca098e4…`; no further compression.\n- **Integrity:** 18 unique thread IDs; 18/18 integrity and command-protocol checks; no timeout, nonzero agent exit, or runner error.\n- **Hashes:** task manifest `f64d4416…`; protocol `0a424ac6…`; raw result `fbe35668…`."},
      {"id":"limitations","type":"markdown","layout":"full","sourceId":"application_results","body":"## Limitations\n\nThe programs remain single-source command-line applications; module boundaries, packages, concurrent work, services, and long-lived repositories remain untested. Six replicates establish a strong direction but not a population estimate across models. Reported tokens include repeated input/context accounting, and rough source tokens are lexical. The file contract proves bytes, not architectural style. One session can repeat a habit across many tasks, so both task and session independence are required."},
      {"id":"decision","type":"markdown","layout":"full","sourceId":"application_results","body":"## Decision\n\n1. Preserve iteration 023 unchanged as a failed 1/4 parity result with complete final correctness.\n2. Make no compiler, grammar, runtime, prompt, or skill change from this corpus.\n3. Preserve raw output, hashes, report inputs, and exact file judgments.\n4. Stop chasing isolated spellings. The next useful engineering target is general first-check discoverability for existing semantics, measured on new tasks—not another alias mined from these transcripts.\n5. Require new unrelated-task recurrence plus general usefulness, semantic consistency, and maintainability before any compiler proposal."}
    ]
  },
